---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import DemoTypeCopy from '../../components/DemoTypeCopy.astro';
import '../../styles/scenario.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="Curb Pickup Assistant | Copilot Studio technical guide">
  <article class="scenario">
    <div class="container">
      <a href={base} class="back">&larr; All scenarios</a>

      <header class="scenario__header">
        <h1>Curb Pickup Assistant</h1>
        <p class="scenario__lead">
          The <strong>Curb Pickup Assistant</strong> combines verified order, store,
          weather, and bay data to recommend a pickup bay. It remembers the plan for
          queue and weather follow-ups and creates a PDF on request.
        </p>
        <div class="scenario__tools">
          <div class="scenario__agent" style="--accent: var(--c-primary);">
            <span class="scenario__agent-icon"><svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2"/><circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2"/><path d="M12 7v4"/><line x1="8" y1="16" x2="8.01" y2="16"/><line x1="16" y1="16" x2="16.01" y2="16"/></svg></span>
            <span class="scenario__agent-text">
              <span class="scenario__agent-label">Test this scenario with</span>
              <span class="scenario__agent-name">Curb Pickup Assistant</span>
            </span>
          </div>
          <DemoTypeCopy />
        </div>
      </header>

      <section class="convo">
        <h2>The conversation</h2>
        <p class="gen-note">
          The customer questions follow a controlled workflow, but the outcome is not
          hardcoded. Store facts, weather, occupancy, and queue values are evaluated
          at runtime. Repeating the same scenario can produce a different bay, wait,
          conditions summary, and recommendation reason.
        </p>

        <aside class="tl-steps demo-orders">
          <p><strong>Try one of these sample orders:</strong></p>
          <p>
            Springfield, IL &mdash; <code>ORD-10421</code> &middot;
            Los Angeles, CA &mdash; <code>ORD-10455</code> &middot;
            Seattle, WA &mdash; <code>ORD-10478</code> &middot;
            Pixel Heights, WA &mdash; <code>ORD-10502</code>
          </p>
          <p>
            To make the verified membership tie-break eligible, use <code>ORD-10502</code> with
            BlastPass ID <code>MEGA-BLAST-1024</code>. Because queues are simulated independently,
            membership affects the result only when the shortest waits are equal.
          </p>
        </aside>

        <ol class="timeline">
          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">1</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">I am collecting order ORD-10502.</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <p>"Do you have a BlastPass? If so, please provide the BlastPass ID."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">2</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">Yes, MEGA-BLAST-1024.</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <p>"Approximately how many minutes until you arrive? You can skip this if you are not sure."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">3</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">About 20 minutes.</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant &rarr; evidence &rarr; recommendation &rarr; optional PDF</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Store Associate Assistant</span> retrieves the order, verifies the customer and shipping address, and returns the exact membership <code>tier_code</code></div>
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Curb Pickup MCP &middot; get_store_location</span> resolves Pixel Heights and returns canonical store metadata with informational local hours</div>
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">MSN Weather</span> retrieves Metric conditions relevant to the customer's expected arrival</div>
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Curb Pickup MCP &middot; list_bays</span> returns one snapshot containing bay attributes, occupancy, 6&ndash;10 orders ahead, and 30-second-per-order wait estimates</div>
                <div class="tl-skill"><span class="tl-skill-name">curbside-bay-selector</span> runs deterministic Python weather, ETA, and queue calculations, reasons over all available bays, and produces the selected bay with structured decision evidence</div>
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Customer response</span> explains how weather, queue, and ETA led to the selected bay, then asks whether the customer wants a PDF copy</div>
                <p>"Rain and darkness favor a covered, well-lit bay. Bay 2 has six orders ahead, about three minutes, leaving time before your arrival. Would you like a copy of the delivery slip?"</p>
                <div class="tl-skill"><span class="tl-skill-name">curbside-slip-pdf</span> runs only after an explicit yes and renders the completed decision without assigning or reserving the bay</div>
                <div class="tl-file"><span class="ticon-cat"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/><line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"/><line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"/></svg></span><span class="ticon-bb">&#129534;</span> returns <strong>blastbox_curbside_slip.pdf</strong> when requested</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">4</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer follow-up</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">Will weather impact my delivery?</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant &rarr; retained recommendation evidence</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Same-session context</span> answers from the existing recommendation without another weather call</div>
                <p>"Yes. Rain and darkness favor the covered, well-lit bay selected for your pickup."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">5</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer follow-up</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">How many orders are ahead of me now?</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant &rarr; remembered state &rarr; updated wait</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Same-session context</span> remembers the assigned bay and original queue start time without fetching another bay snapshot</div>
                <div class="tl-skill"><span class="tl-skill-name">curbside-bay-selector</span> calculates progress from that start at one order every 30 seconds and returns the remaining wait with an estimated curb-ready time</div>
                <p>"There are now five orders ahead. About 2 minutes 30 seconds remains, with curb-ready estimated for 10:24 AM."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-user">
            <div class="tl-marker">6</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Customer follow-up</div>
              <div class="try-prompt">
                <blockquote class="try-prompt__text">How much longer is the current wait?</blockquote>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>

          <li class="tl-agent">
            <div class="tl-marker">&#9670;</div>
            <div class="tl-content">
              <div class="tl-label">Curb Pickup Assistant &rarr; previous update time &rarr; recalculated curb-ready time</div>
              <div class="tl-steps">
                <div class="tl-tool"><span class="tl-tool-name">Context memory</span> carries forward the timestamp from the preceding queue update</div>
                <div class="tl-skill"><span class="tl-skill-name">Queue response</span> reports the remembered update time, current orders ahead, remaining wait, and new estimated curb-ready time</div>
                <p>"Since your last update at 10:21 AM, there are now four orders ahead. About two minutes remains, with curb-ready estimated for 10:24 AM."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="result">
          <span class="result__icon"><span class="ticon-cat"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 21h18"/><path d="M5 21V10l7-7 7 7v11"/><path d="M9 21v-6h6v6"/></svg></span><span class="ticon-bb">&#128663;</span></span>
          <div>
            <div class="result__label">Agentic pickup recommendation with optional PDF</div>
            <div class="result__value">Live API reasoning &middot; context memory &middot; follow-up reasoning &middot; optional PDF</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="scenario__section">
        <h2>What was demonstrated</h2>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <div class="value-card">
            <h3>Collects live and business data</h3>
            <p>The agent combines verified order and membership data with live store, weather, bay, occupancy, and queue facts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="value-card">
            <h3>Reasons over the combined data</h3>
            <p>It evaluates weather suitability, availability, queue, ETA, and membership tie-breaks to select and explain one bay.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="value-card">
            <h3>Presents a clear response</h3>
            <p>It connects the evidence to the recommendation, gives practical pickup guidance, and creates the delivery-slip PDF only when requested.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="value-card">
            <h3>Remembers and reuses context</h3>
            <p>It retains queue timing and recommendation evidence to recalculate waits and answer later questions without repeating unnecessary data calls.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="scenario__section">
        <h2>What gets generated</h2>
        <p>
          File generation is an optional presentation step, not the decision mechanism.
          After the agent presents its recommendation and the customer asks for a PDF,
          <code>curbside-slip-pdf</code> renders the selected bay, live conditions,
          current queue, estimated wait, optional ETA comparison, and recommendation
          reason.
        </p>
        <a class="filecard filecard--download" href={`${base}files/blastbox_curbside_slip.pdf`} download>
          <span class="filecard__icon">&#128196;</span>
          <span class="filecard__body">
            <strong>blastbox_curbside_slip.pdf</strong>
            <small>Download the illustrative recommendation PDF</small>
          </span>
          <span class="filecard__action">Download</span>
        </a>
        <figure class="slip-preview">
          <a href={`${base}files/blastbox_curbside_slip.pdf`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img
              src={`${base}img/blastbox_curbside_slip-preview.png`}
              alt="BlastBox curb pickup recommendation PDF for Jordan Pixel and order ORD-10502, showing recommended Bay 2, queue timing, weather conditions, and the reason for the recommendation."
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </a>
          <figcaption>Illustrative output from the optional PDF skill.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
